From: Petru Mare <43178362+Petru101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mf/sar: Don't request samples after the clock is stopped.

MonoGame 3.7.1 (MediaPlayer.WMS.cs) resets a finished song with Start(0)
followed right away by Stop(). After OnClockStop, the render callback can
still run once from the audio client's buffer event; it found the queue
empty and queued MEStreamSinkRequestSample without looking at the clock
state, unlike the ProcessSample path. The session took that request while
stopped and counted it as pending in the decoder node, the source dropped
it when it was started again from a position, and on the next Start of the
same presentation nothing was requested from the source any more: the
music stopped for good (Picross for a Cause).

Only request a sample while the clock isn't stopped, or while prerolling:
the renderer keeps requesting samples during preroll with the clock
stopped (test_sar_time_source), and SAR_PREROLLED is cleared by
OnClockStop.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mf/sar.c b/dlls/mf/sar.c
index e7569897..c8ce47c4 100644
--- a/dlls/mf/sar.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/sar.c
@@ -2149,7 +2149,8 @@ static void audio_renderer_render(struct audio_renderer *renderer, IMFAsyncResul
 
     if (list_empty(&renderer->queue))
     {
-        if (!(renderer->flags & SAR_SAMPLE_REQUESTED))
+        if (!(renderer->flags & SAR_SAMPLE_REQUESTED)
+                && (renderer->clock_state != MFCLOCK_STATE_STOPPED || renderer->flags & SAR_PREROLLED))
         {
             IMFMediaEventQueue_QueueEventParamVar(renderer->stream_event_queue, MEStreamSinkRequestSample, &GUID_NULL, S_OK, NULL);
             renderer->flags |= SAR_SAMPLE_REQUESTED;
